@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="spacer"></div>
<div class="row p-3">
    <ul class="breadcrumb w-100 p-2 m-0 link-normal">
        <li class="breadcrumb-item">
            <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index">
                <i class="fas fa-home me-1"></i>Home
            </a>
        </li>
        <li class="breadcrumb-item active">
            <a href="#">
                @ViewData["Title"]
            </a>
        </li>
    </ul>
</div>

<h1 class="mt-2 mb-4">@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<p>
    This Privacy Policy explains our policies and practices for collecting, using, and disclosing Your information while using the
    service, as well as your privacy rights and how the law protects you.
</p>
<p>

    Your personal information is used to offer and improve the service.<br /><br />
    <b>You agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this Privacy Policy by using the service.</b>
</p>

<h3 class="mt-3 col-12 px-0">1. Definitions</h3>
<ul>
    <li><p>Account refers to a one-of-a-kind account created for you to use to access our service or parts of it. </p></li>
    <li>
        <p>
            Nilu Digital Store (referred to as either "We", "Us" or "Our" in this agreement) refers to Nilu Digital Store,
            Sarker Bari, Paramtala-3540, Muradnagar upazill, Cumilla, Bangladesh.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            Cookies are little data that a website saves on your computer, mobile device, or other device, and which save information
            about your shopping cart, browsing history etc. on that website among its many uses.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li><p>Personal data is any information that can be used to identify or contact a specific person. </p></li>
    <li><p>Any gadget that may access the service, such as a computer, a cellphone, or a digital tablet, is referred to as a device.</p></li>
    <li><p>Service refers to the website. Website refers to Nilu Digital Store, accessible from https://niludigital.com</p></li>
    <li>
        <p>
            Any general or legal person who processes data on behalf of the company is referred to as a service provider.
            It refers to third-party companies or individuals hired by the company to enable the service, deliver the service on the company's
            behalf, conduct related services, or assist the company in assessing how the service is utilized.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li><p>Data gathered automatically as a result of using the service or from the service infrastructure itself is referred to as usage data.</p></li>
    <li><p>You refers to the person accessing or using the service, as well as the company or other legal organization on whose behalf such person is accessing or using the service. </p></li>
</ul>
<p>
    Nilu Digital Store understands how important your privacy and the use of your personal information are to you.
    Our Privacy Policy is described in this notice.
    This Privacy Policy applies to information we collect about you from any source and in any way, including our Websites,
    applications, and other Internet-based interactions.
</p>

<p>
    <b>
        Nilu Digital Store processes personal data in line with applicable laws, including Bangladesh's Digital Security Act, 2018,
        the Section 26 of which specifies protection for personal data processing and free movement of such data.
    </b>
</p>

<h3 class="mt-3 col-12 px-0">2. Information Collection</h3>
<p>We collect the following personal data from our visitors and customers: </p>
<ul>
    <li>
        <p>
            Any information you enter on our Websites or give us in any other manner is received and stored by us.
            You can choose not to supply certain information, but you will be unable to purchase anything provided on the website or
            take advantage of certain services or promotions if you do so.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            When you place an order with us online, your contact information is used to connect with you via email for necessary operations
            such as order processing and invoicing, transferring deliverables and necessary transaction information is stored for resolving
            possible disputes. By canceling your order, you can opt-out of these emails and processes.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            When you create an account, make a purchase, contact us, submit content on our website, or subscribe to our newsletter,
            we collect information about you. Name, address, email address, and phone numbers are the most common pieces of
            information collected.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            Your IP address, login and password information, email address, web browser type and version, operating system and computer platform, purchase history, which we may aggregate with similar information from other guests or keep in non-aggregated form, through, and from our website, including date and time one or more unique identifiers, products you viewed or searched for are among the types of information we receive or can determine from your interaction with our website.
            We may also keep track of the length of your visit and the number of times you visit and buy something from us.
            To keep track of your future visits, we may assign you one or more unique identifiers.<br />


            If you want to remove  information collected, please email us at <b>support@niludigital.com</b>.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li><p>Usage Data is collected automatically when using the service.</p></li>
</ul>

<h3 class="mt-3 col-12 px-0">3. Purpose and Use of Information Collection</h3>
<p>We may use personal data for the following purposes:</p>
<ul>
    <li><p>To provide and maintain our service, including monitoring its uses.</p></li>
    <li>
        <p>
            To manage your account as a registered user. The personal information you provide may grant you access to various features of the service
            that are available to you.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li><p>To communicate with you via email, phone calls, text messages, or other similar electronic means.</p></li>
    <li>
        <p>
            Unless you have opted not to receive such information, to send you news, special offers, and general information about other
            goods, services, and events that we offer that are similar to those you have already purchased or inquired about.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            We may use your information to evaluate or carry out a merger, divestiture, restructuring, reorganization, dissolution,
            or other sale or transfer of some or all of our assets, whether as a going concern or as part of a bankruptcy, liquidation,
            or similar proceeding, in which personal data about our service users is one of the assets transferred.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            We may also use your information for data analysis, identifying usage trends, determining the effectiveness of our promotional
            campaigns, and evaluating and improving our service, products, services, marketing, and your experience.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li><p></p></li>
</ul>

<h3 class="mt-3 col-12 px-0">4. Sharing of Information</h3>
<p>We may share your personal information in the following situations:</p>
<ul>
    <li>
        <p>
            We may disclose information to respond to subpoenas, court orders, legal process, law enforcement requests,
            legal claims or government inquiries, and to protect and defend the rights, interests, health, safety, and security of
            Nilu Digital Store, our affiliates, users, or the public.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            Your information may be shared with third-party vendors and service providers who assist us with specialized services such
            as billing, payment processing, customer service, email deployment, business analytics, marketing, advertising,
            performance monitoring, hosting, and data processing.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            We may share your information in the course of a significant corporate transaction, such as
            a merger, consolidation, asset sale, or the unlikely event of bankruptcy.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li><p>We may share your information with our corporate affiliates that are subject to this policy.</p></li>
    <li><p>We may share information for any other purpose disclosed to you at the time of collection or with your consent or direction. </p></li>
</ul>

<h3 class="mt-3 col-12 px-0">5. Security</h3>
<p>
    We take reasonable precautions to safeguard information against loss, theft, misuse, and unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration,
    and destruction. It is important to understand that no data storage system or data transmission over the Internet or any other public
    network can be guaranteed to be completely secure. Please keep in mind that information collected by third parties may not be subject
    to the same security safeguards as information you provide to us, and we are not responsible for the security of such information.
</p>


<h3 class="mt-3 col-12 px-0">6. Your Choices</h3>
<ul>
    <li>
        <p>
            You can unsubscribe from our email newsletters by clicking the "unsubscribe" link at the bottom of each newsletter and following the instructions.
            You may also opt out of all Nilu Digital Store communications by contacting us via <b>support@niludigital.com</b>.
        </p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p>
            By adjusting your web browser settings, you may be able to refuse or disable cookies. It may prevent you from availing some
            services such as remembering logins, shopping cart sync etc.
            Because each web browser is unique, please refer to the instructions that came with your web browser.
        </p>
    </li>
</ul>

<h3 class="mt-3 col-12 px-0">7. Cookies</h3>
<p>
    We use cookies and similar technologies for technical reasons to ensure the website's efficient operation,
    to improve the website's ease of use, and to collect statistics on how you use our website.
    By using the website, you agree to the use of cookies and other similar technologies by us.
    You may opt out of cookies and similar technologies as described in the "Your Choices" section above,
    but please keep in mind that if you do, certain features of the website may cease to function for you.
</p>


<h3 class="mt-3 col-12 px-0">8. Changes to the Privacy Policy</h3>
<p>
    We reserve the right to make changes to this Privacy Policy at any time.
    When we update the Policy, we will revise the "Effective Data" date below and post the new Privacy Policy.
    We recommend that you read the Privacy Policy each time you visit the Sites to stay up to date on our privacy practices.
</p>

<p class="mt-3"><b>Effective Data: January 01, 2022</b></p>
